<p>For Canadian businesses specifically, DBNAlliance offers a genuine structured exchange option using the OASIS UBL format — the same underlying standard used by several other countries in this tracker — without waiting for any federal mandate that doesn''t yet exist. Registration works through a DBNAlliance Access Point, an online platform handling both sending and receiving of compliant e-invoices on a business''s behalf, in a model deliberately similar to how Peppol access points function in Europe.</p>
<p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if your business trades heavily with US counterparties, or simply wants genuine structured invoicing efficiency without waiting for a Canadian mandate that may be years away, DBNAlliance is worth evaluating now as a voluntary option rather than treating structured e-invoicing as something only relevant once a domestic law requires it. Given the momentum building through 2026''s conferences and onboarding sessions, this network is genuinely maturing, not merely a paper initiative.</p>');
INSERT INTO stories (id, date, month, summary_en, html_en, source_url, published) VALUES ('2026-02-01-canada-provincial-federal-exploration', '2026-02-01', '2026-02', 'While no Canadian domestic e-invoicing mandate has been announced, Quebec has shown active interest in sector-specific e-reporting models, and a federal E-Invoicing Advisory Group task force continues studying feasibility across all levels of government.', '<h3>🇨🇦 No domestic mandate yet, but Quebec and a federal task force are actively exploring one</h3>
<p>Canada''s lack of a domestic B2B e-invoicing mandate is a genuine outlier internationally — as a G7 and OECD member closely tied to jurisdictions that have already moved significantly on tax digitalisation, the absence of federal regulation here looks more like an exception than a stable long-term position. Worth knowing directly rather than assuming nothing is happening: the federal government has established an E-Invoicing Advisory Group task force specifically to study the feasibility of e-invoicing across all levels of Canadian government, not just at the federal level where the existing SAP Ariba requirement already applies.</p>
<p>At the provincial level, Quebec has shown genuine, specific interest in electronic reporting models for particular sectors — a notably more concrete signal than general policy discussion, though still short of an actual announced mandate. Combined with private-sector momentum already building around EDI adoption in retail and pharmaceutical trade, and Canada''s participation in international forums like the OECD''s Forum on Tax Administration, the overall direction points toward eventual convergence with international standards — even without a specific date attached to that direction yet.</p>
<p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> treat the absence of a Canadian domestic mandate as a genuinely temporary state rather than a stable long-term policy position — the exploratory work already underway, both federally and in Quebec specifically, suggests this is a matter of when rather than if. Businesses with meaningful Quebec operations in particular may want to track that province''s own sector-specific initiatives more closely than the general national conversation, since provincial movement could arrive before any federal B2B mandate does.</p>', 'https://www.canada.ca/en/public-services-procurement.html', 1);
INSERT INTO story_countries (story_id, country_id) SELECT '2026-02-01-canada-provincial-federal-exploration', id FROM countries WHERE name_en = 'Canada';
